xnu 0302: blank the panel when the display sleeps

CoreAnimation stops swapping when the screen sleeps, and this driver has no
power call to hear it, so a quiet compositor is the signal. After
mondrianfb_blank seconds (default 3) without a present the display tick paints
the panel memory black; the CTL start it already issues sends that frame, and
black is what an AMOLED shows when it is off. A sleeping compositor still
presents the occasional lone frame, so a wake needs a burst (3 presents inside
1.5 s) and the lone ones leave the black frame in place. mondrianfb_blank=0
disables the timeout.

Measured: locked, the compositor presents 0/s while the panel keeps the last
frame (panel 0/60 sampled ticks changed); on, it presents 54-60/s even with no
touch, so the timeout separates sleep from a still screen. Housekeeping frames
arrive about every four seconds while asleep; treating any present as a wake
blinked the panel, hence the burst test.

